# Normalize line endings: store LF in the repository, check out LF everywhere.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks files out as CRLF
# while Prettier defaults to `endOfLine: "lf"`, so `npx prettier --check` reports
# every source file as unformatted — including files just written by
# `prettier --write`. See "Known rough edges" in AGENTS.md.
#
# `text=auto` leaves binary files (public/images/*) alone; git detects them by
# content rather than trusting the extension.
* text=auto eol=lf
